  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-LBN103</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of constituents for developing  inclusive, sustainable and resilient skills and lifelong learning systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon&#x2019;s TVET system faces persistent challenges linked to outdated governance, weak labour market intelligence, limited private sector engagement, outdated curricula, and reduced access and quality as a result of the economic crisis and recent hostilities. During the biennium, the ILO will support the strengthening of a more inclusive, market-responsive and resilient TVET system that improves young people&#x2019;s access to quality skills and facilitates transitions to decent and productive employment. Expected results include an updated National Strategic Framework for TVET for 2025&#x2013;2029; improved evidence on youth and community perceptions of TVET; strengthened national capacity to conduct graduate tracer studies; and the development and validation of curricula that better reflect labour market needs, including through closer cooperation with the industrial sector and exploration of public-private partnerships. Beneficiaries include young women and men, TVET students and graduates, vulnerable youth, public TVET institutions, employers and workers requiring relevant skills for evolving labour market demand. The strategy will be implemented with relevant government institutions, public TVET bodies, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, industrial sector stakeholders, education and training institutions, UN agencies and development partners, in support of inclusive skills development, employability and improved employment outcomes for youth in Lebanon.</narrative>
  </description>
